00:00:01,060 --> 00:00:02,530
D2.

2
00:00:02,530 --> 00:00:07,945
Read Millie's article for Teenagers Magazine.

3
00:00:07,945 --> 00:00:12,335
Practice makes perfect.

4
00:00:12,335 --> 00:00:23,300
A year ago, when I wanted to share my ideas in an English class, I could not express myself well.

5
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:30,670
I felt sorry about that, so I made a plan to improve my English.

6
00:00:30,670 --> 00:00:38,310
I listened to English on a language learning app every morning after I got up.

7
00:00:38,310 --> 00:00:44,140
I also repeated the sentences to improve my pronunciation.

8
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:48,330
The app helped me correct my mistakes.

9
00:00:48,330 --> 00:00:55,480
What's more, I practiced speaking English with my classmates at school.

10
00:00:55,480 --> 00:01:06,060
Several months later, my English became much better and I was not afraid of speaking English anymore.

11
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:08,910
Practice makes perfect.

12
00:01:08,910 --> 00:01:14,540
Now I am happy that I can express myself well in English.
